<title>AUSTRALIA: AWB sells no wheat at 21st domestic wheat tender.</title>
<headline>AWB sells no wheat at 21st domestic wheat tender.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Australian Wheat Board (AWB) said it sold no wheat at its 21st tender for the sale of wheat on the domestic market on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The total amount bid for in the tender was 18,000 tonnes of nearby wheat and 6,000 tonnes of new crop 1997/98 season wheat.</p>
<p>Closing date for the next tender is April 30.  </p>
<p>Highest unsuccessful offers in 21st tender:</p>
<p>    Port	   Grade	    Highest failed bid A$/t</p>
<p>					  Nearby	   New crop</p>
<p>    Newcastle    ASW		189.00	   186.50</p>
<p>    Port Kembla  ASW		189.00</p>
<p>    Port Kembla  Feed	     178.00</p>
<p>    Geelong	ASW		194.00</p>
<p>    Geelong	Feed	     170.00</p>
<p>	  -- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
